From c30a91bb1ef5d276fa04b633cbec50f46b0b32c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mark-vis <118430440+mark-vis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 15:43:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 03/14] Skip the arguments of \caption outside a float

After the error "\caption outside float", \caption now skips the star,
the optional and the mandatory argument. Before, only the following
group was gobbled, so the caption text was typeset. The rest of
\caption is still removed expandably and the skipping command is
protected, so \caption outside a float still expands without errors in
an expansion context; github-robust-0123 now shows
\@caption@skip@star before the argument. tlb2815 is unchanged (it
defines its own \caption).

\caption is now in a release block ("caption arguments", the name the
block keeps when later changes add to it); the roll-back and hook-list
.tlg files list it. New test caption-outside-001.

Packages that define their own \caption are not changed by this: the
redefinition in latex-lab-float (tagging) still only gobbles the next
group (it is removed when the kernel \caption gets the socket
caption/step), and hyperref (without \DocumentMetadata) and float.sty
define \caption with \expandafter\@gobble as well, so with them the
caption text outside a float is still typeset.

This change is optional and independent of the rest of the series.
